  [1m[38;5;153mapp.js[39m becomes a module.[0m [38;5;153mindex.html:13[39m changes to [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m, and [38;5;153mapp.js[39m gains one import:

  [34mimport[39m { getVisitorId } [34mfrom[39m [31m"./src/visitor-id.js"[39m;

  Two consequences worth naming. [38;5;153mlogin[39m, [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m, and [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m stop being globals — nothing in the repo
  references them from outside [38;5;153mapp.js[39m, so nothing breaks, but anything poking at them from the browser console would
  need to change. And module scripts are deferred, so the top-level [38;5;153mdocument.getElementById("login-form")[39m now runs after
  the DOM is parsed rather than racing it — a small correctness win.

  [1mThe signature change[0m you asked for, as an optional third parameter:

  [34mfunction[39m [33mlogin[39m(username, password, userId = [34mnull[39m) {
    console.[33mlog[39m([31m"Logging in:"[39m, username, [31m"visitor:"[39m, userId);
    [32m// Stub: would POST to API_ENDPOINT in real app[39m
    [34mreturn[39m { [36msuccess[39m: [34mtrue[39m, [36muser[39m: username, userId };
  }

  Defaulting to [38;5;153mnull[39m means any caller that hasn't been updated keeps working and gets an explicit [38;5;153mnull[39m rather than
  [38;5;153mundefined[39m.

  [1mThe one call site[0m ([38;5;153mapp.js:23[39m) becomes [38;5;153mlogin(username, password, getVisitorId())[39m.

  I'd resolve the ID at the call site rather than inside [38;5;153mlogin()[39m on purpose: [38;5;153mlogin()[39m stays a function of its arguments,
  which keeps it testable and keeps it honest when you later wire up the real [38;5;153mfetch[39m. The alternative — [38;5;153mlogin()[39m reaching
  for the ID itself — would make the parameter you asked for pointless.

  [1m[38;5;153mREADME.md[0m picks up a short "running locally" line, since opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by double-clicking will now fail with a
  CORS error on the module script. That failure is silent-ish in the console and worth documenting.

  [1mNot in scope:[0m no change to [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m, no change to [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m or [38;5;153msrc/utils.js[39m (they stay CommonJS and stay
  unreferenced by the page), and no [38;5;153mfetch[39m implementation — [38;5;153mlogin()[39m remains a stub.

